=== PARITY (web source reproduced end-to-end) ===
  - Data sources: NONE (web "no API data sources — renders from navigation values /
    local state"). The page is local-only; there is no loading/empty/error data-state
    to model. The single declared `success` state is the curated catalog's loaded rows,
    bound via SqlPlaygroundPageModel.catalogState = .success([CuratedTable]).
  - Panel 1 (web GlassPanel1 — Manual SQL editor): TSGlassPanel → TSPanelTitle +
    TSTextArea(text:$model.sql) (empty-field prompt overlay, a11y label/value) +
    Run/Clear (TSButton, disabled when !canRun) + deterministic run-status message.
    Run mirrors web handleRun: empty input → editorRunEmpty hint; otherwise →
    editorRunUnavailable guidance (the page exposes NO execution endpoint, exactly
    like web). Clear mirrors handleClear. Draft persists on change + is removed when
    emptied (web localStorage useEffect), key "ai.sqlPlayground.draft".
  - Panel 2 (web GlassPanel2 — Curated schema catalog): TSGlassPanel → TSPanelTitle +
    intro + the 5 curated tables (drives, charging_sessions, vehicles, alerts,
    signal_log_view) ALPHABETIZED (web sortedTables), each a card with mono table name
    (accent), summary, and an adaptive 1→2 column grid of `name · type — summary`
    (web grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2). Table/column identifiers + summaries render
    verbatim, exactly as the web CURATED_CATALOG constant renders them (schema data,
    not localized chrome). Columns are SI-canonical (distance_m/duration_s/energy_used_wh/
    avg_speed_mps/max_speed_mps; energy_added_wh; max_power_w) — no legacy unit suffix.
  - i18n: all 11 powerSql.* keys preserved verbatim from the web source, resolved via
    LocalizedStringKey from the central Localizable.xcstrings (same mechanism as the
    registered AppSettingsView). Catalog English values inserted into the catalog.
    NO hardcoded user-facing chrome literals in the view (all via SqlPlaygroundStrings).
  - Accessibility: VoiceOver labels on the editor (label + value), Run/Clear, the
    run-status message (static-text live region), each table card (combined name+summary),
    and each column row (combined name/type/summary); Dynamic-Type system fonts (Font.TS);
    light/dark + increased-contrast via Color.TS dynamic colors; ≥44pt targets (TSButton).
  - Navigation: `.powerUser` route host → PowerUserHubView (HIG List) → push
    SqlPlaygroundPage via .navigationDestination(for: PowerUserDestination). Adaptive
    NavigationSplitView (macOS/iPad) + NavigationStack (iPhone) supplied by AppShell.
  - Telemetry (P1/S11): SqlPlaygroundPageModel.start() emits view.opened with surface
    slug "SqlPlaygroundPage" exactly once (OSLog default; prod injects shared adapter);
    user SQL is never logged.
  - AI drafter (web AINLSqlPlayground): feature-flagged + NOT in this parity unit's
    manifest (no AI panel/string declared) → intentionally out of scope (ADR-015 I5
    "hidden in off-mode"); the model keeps an applyDraft() seam for the propose-only path.

